// Runtime/MailboxRuntime.maxon — the MAILBOX a service receives on, and the four handle/lifetime doors
// around it. The spec is `specs/services.md`: §"Sending MOVES, and that is load-bearing" for
// the ownership rule, §"Shutdown" for the close-after-drain and the last-handle close.
//
// ⭐⭐ **A MAILBOX IS A RING OF MESSAGE SLOTS, A ONE-SLOT INBOX, A SENDER QUEUE AND TWO REFERENCE
// COUNTS, AND NOTHING ELSE.** A send copies the message into the inbox of a parked receiver or
// of one that has never run, or into the ring's tail, and returns; a receive answers the inbox,
// copying the ring's head slot into it when no first message waits there, or PARKS; a close
// makes the queue drainable and un-fillable. A mailbox whose receiver never runs cuts no ring.
// A send given a timeout to a full mailbox parks on the FIFO sender queue (Go's `sendq`): the
// receive that frees a slot moves the first waiting sender's message into it and readies that
// sender, and a close readies every waiting sender `stopped`. No message is ever a heap record.
// What makes it more than a queue is the pair of counts: `handles` is how many `<T>.handle`
// boxes name it (the last one to go CLOSES it, which is the whole of "an ordinary program needs
// no shutdown boilerplate"), and `refs` is that plus the loop itself (the last one to go FREES
// it, which is what lets the loop outlive the handles it is draining for).
//
// ⚠ Every message buffer lives off the green-thread stack. The ring and the parked-receiver copy
// are Go's `hchan` buffer and `sendDirect`, but Go copies to and from goroutine stacks and adjusts
// those pointers through precise stack maps when `copystack` moves one. A green thread's stack
// moves here too and only its sp/fp and saved-fp chain are rebased, so a stack address held across
// a park or a guarded call goes stale. The sender builds the message in its thread's staging buffer
// (`MboxStagingName`) and the receiver reads it from the inbox in this region; a waiting sender's
// message stays in that buffer until the receive moves it.
//
// ⭐⭐ **NO NEW `.data` WORD, AND THAT IS A LAYOUT ARGUMENT AS WELL AS A DESIGN ONE.** Mailbox state
// is per-STRUCT, in the heap, reached from the handle box. A `.data` word would need a
// `MultiMSharing` class (`SchedRuntime.pushRuntimeGlobal` PANICS without one) and would shift every
// label after it, moving **every heap program's `data {` table** — `SlabRuntime`'s own header
// records that cost for the allocator's lock, which lives in its state region for exactly this
// reason.
//
// ⚠ BOTH PARKS CARRY THE MAILBOX LOCK ACROSS `__gt_context_switch`. `__mbox_recv` publishes itself
// as `parkedGt`, and `__mbox_send_queue` appends itself to the sender queue, and each parks holding
// the lock; `__gt_run_strand` leaves it in the park commit (`emitMboxParkCommit`,
// `emitMboxSendParkCommit`) on the same OS thread, before that thread runs any other green thread.
// The lock is exclusive, so a green thread run there while the hold was still open would wait for
// ever on a holder that cannot run.
//
// ring, ringSlots, head, count, parkedGt, closed, receiver and the sender queue are read and
// written only under the mailbox lock, because `__mbox_recv`'s decision to park rests on "empty,
// open and nobody parked" being one instant across three words. The two counts share one atomic
// word outside the lock (`MboxOffShares`).
let MboxOffRing = 0x00
let MboxOffRingSlots = 0x08
let MboxOffHead = 0x10
let MboxOffCount = 0x18

// ⚠ **NAMED `parkedGt` AND NOT `waiter`, BECAUSE `GtOffWaiter` IS A DIFFERENT FACT ABOUT THE SAME THREAD.**
// A GT's `waiter` is the scheduler context that switched it in — who to context-switch back to.
// This is the green thread parked in `__mbox_recv` on THIS mailbox, i.e. who to make `ready` when a
// request arrives. Two fields called `waiter` in one wake sequence is exactly the confusion that
// writes a status into the wrong struct.
let MboxOffParkedGt = 0x20

// Non-zero once the mailbox has been closed — by the last handle drop, or by `h.shutdown()`. A send
// to a closed mailbox is refused with `stopped` rather than queued, and a receive on a closed EMPTY
// one answers 0, which is how the loop learns to exit.
let MboxOffClosed = 0x28

// `handles` in the high 32 bits and `refs` in the low 32, so a mint steps both in one `lock xadd` of
// `MboxShareUnit`. The loop's exit frees on a prior of exactly `MboxLastRefOnly`, which any live
// handle's bits rule out.
let MboxOffShares = 0x30

// The concrete service's request-union size, stored at spawn: the ring's stride and a receive's
// copy length. A send copies only its own `bytes`, which an interface send can make smaller, so
// `bytes` is never the stride.
let MboxOffSlotBytes = 0x38

// The `spawn`'s capacity. The capacity need not be a power of two: `full` compares the messages
// held, `count` plus an `inboxQueued` inbox's one, against it and never against `ringSlots`, which
// doubling keeps a power of two and so may exceed it.
let MboxOffCapacity = 0x40

// A `MboxReceiverState`. The inbox belongs to the receiver from a receive's return until its
// next receive, and every receive holds the lock until it returns or commits a park, so with no
// receiver parked the inbox is free to fill only while `fresh`: the receiver has never entered
// `__mbox_recv`. While `inboxQueued`, the inbox holds a message that `count`, the ring's
// length, does not include.
let MboxOffReceiver = 0x48

// The sender queue's root: `mbox + MboxSendRootBias` reads as a GT whose `GtOffSendNext` and
// `GtOffSendPrev` are these two words, so the circular list has no empty case. ⚠ The two must stay
// one word apart, as the GT's pair is, or a link store through the root lands in another field.
let MboxOffSendNext = 0x50
let MboxOffSendPrev = MboxOffSendNext + PointerFieldBytes
let MboxSendRootBias = MboxOffSendNext - GtOffSendNext

// Taken before `__sched_lock`, never under it. Inside its hold: `__gt_run_strand` may shrink a
// parked receiver's stack, which takes the stack-pool lock; the ring's scaffold alloc and free run;
// and arming a waiting sender's timer takes `__sched_lock`. A receiver's ready, and a claimed
// sender's, runs after the leave. Neither the stack pool, the allocator nor a `__sched_lock`
// holder takes a mailbox lock, so a path that took this lock under any of them would deadlock.
let MboxOffLock = (MboxOffSendPrev + PointerFieldBytes) as ByteOffset
let MboxHeaderBytes = (MboxOffLock as FullRangeInt) + ExclusiveLockBytes
let MboxOffInbox = MboxHeaderBytes as ByteOffset

// A power of two, kept one by doubling: a slot index is `& (ringSlots - 1)`. A capacity at or
// below it seeds a ring that holds it whole, so only a ring whose capacity exceeds it grows: the
// receive's `ringSlots > MboxInitialSlots` test means grown, and a shrink reseeds at this size.
let MboxInitialSlots = 16
let MboxSlotGrowth = 2
let MboxRingHeadReset = 0
let MboxInboxHeldMessages = 1

enum MboxReceiverState
	fresh = 0
	inboxQueued = 1
	started = 2
end 'MboxReceiverState'

enum MboxTakeSource
	ring = 0
	inbox = 1
end 'MboxTakeSource'

let MboxClosedAndDrained = 0

// The two counts' initial values, named because they are a PAIR and their difference is the whole lifetime
// rule: one handle names the mailbox, and the loop is the second thing that keeps it alive.
let MboxInitialHandles = 1
let MboxInitialRefs = 2
let MboxHandleShift = 32 as FullRangeInt
let MboxHandleUnit = 1 shl MboxHandleShift
let MboxRefUnit = 1
module let MboxShareUnit = MboxHandleUnit + MboxRefUnit
let MboxInitialShares = MboxInitialHandles * MboxHandleUnit + MboxInitialRefs * MboxRefUnit
let MboxLastRefOnly = MboxRefUnit
let MboxSoleHandle = 1

// The value stored into `closed`. Any non-zero would do; the constant is what stops a reader spelling `1`
// and a writer spelling something else.
let MboxIsClosed = 1

let MboxNoHandedMessage = 0
let MboxChainEnd = 0
let MboxHandedMessage = 1

export enum MboxSendWake
	pending = 0
	delivered = 1
	cancelled = 2
	stopped = 3
	timedOut = 4
end 'MboxSendWake'

export enum MboxSendStatus
	delivered = 0
	full = 1
	stopped = 2
end 'MboxSendStatus'

// --- Entry points ---

// ⭐⭐ **`__svc_spawn(loopPtr, state, slotBytes, capacity) -> mbox` — CREATE THE MAILBOX AND THE
// GREEN THREAD THAT SERVES IT, IN THAT ORDER.** The mailbox exists before the thread does, because
// the thread's second argument IS the mailbox; and the thread is published LAST, once both its
// argument slots are written, for `GtRuntime.GtReadyName`'s measured reason (a worker M dequeues
// and runs a spawned thread while the spawning thread is still storing its arguments).
//
// ⚠ **IT ANSWERS THE MAILBOX AND NOT A HANDLE BOX.** The `<T>.handle` box is allocated by the PARSER, at
// `emitBoxAlloc` — the one `__mm_alloc` door, which is where the box header's destructor argument is decided
// — and this pointer is stored into its one field. A runtime-minted box would be a second place that knows
// what a managed record costs.
export let SvcSpawnName = b"__svc_spawn"

// `__mbox_send(mbox, msg, bytes, timeoutMs)` — copy `bytes` of one staged request into the
// inbox of a parked or never-run receiver or the ring's tail, or answer
// `MboxSendStatus.stopped` / `.full` if it cannot.
// With `timeoutMs` 0 a full mailbox answers `full` at once and the send never suspends. Otherwise
// the sender waits on the sender queue until a receive moves its message (`delivered`), a close
// (`stopped`), its deadline or a dropped promise (`full`). It is NOT on `SemanticCheck`'s park
// roster: whether a send can park is the `serviceSend` op's `timed` bit, which `opYields` reads.
export let MboxSendName = b"__mbox_send"

// `__mbox_send_queue(mbox, msg, bytes, timeoutMs)` — the rest of `__mbox_send`: an append behind
// an `inboxQueued` inbox, a ring seed or growth, and a full mailbox's refusal or wait. It is a
// function of its own so that its frame is not `__mbox_send`'s, whose prologue every send pays on
// a cold green stack before the lock is taken. It is entered holding the mailbox lock with the
// receiver `started` or `inboxQueued`, and leaves the lock on every road.
let MboxSendQueueName = b"__mbox_send_queue"

// `__mbox_recv_take(mbox, source) -> inbox` — the rest of `__mbox_recv`, apart for
// `MboxSendQueueName`'s reason: a take that admits a waiting sender, or that drains a grown ring
// and shrinks it. It is entered holding the mailbox lock and leaves it.
let MboxRecvTakeName = b"__mbox_recv_take"

// `__mbox_staging() -> record` — the calling green thread's message buffer, sized to the program's
// largest request union. It is carved from the scheduler's uncounted arena at the thread's first
// send and kept in `GtRuntime.GtOffStaging` for the record's life. A thread has one, which
// `Parser.emitServiceSendOp` states the consequence of.
export let MboxStagingName = b"__mbox_staging"

// ⭐ `__mbox_recv(mbox) -> inbox | 0` — the loop's only blocking operation, and the one mailbox
// entry that IS a park point. It answers 0 exactly once: when the mailbox is closed AND drained.
// The inbox holds the message until this thread's next receive, because a send copies into it only
// while this thread is parked here or has never entered here (`MboxOffReceiver`).
export let MboxRecvName = b"__mbox_recv"

// EXPORTED because `h.shutdown()` closes the mailbox while its handles are still alive — the close is what
// lets the loop drain what is queued and then exit.
export let MboxCloseName = b"__mbox_close"

// `__mbox_send_abandon(gt) -> wakeDebt` — `GtRuntime.buildGtPromiseDrop`'s answer to a coroutine
// parked in a send: take it off its mailbox's sender queue and ready it `cancelled`, so its send
// answers `full` and hands the arguments back. A sender another waker has claimed belongs to it,
// and is left alone.
export let MboxSendAbandonName = b"__mbox_send_abandon"

// `__mbox_handle_clone_box(handleBox) -> handleBox` — a second HANDLE to the SAME service, never a second
// service. Exported because `SignatureIndex.managedNameCascadeStrategy` routes `<T>.handle`'s clone here.
export let MboxHandleCloneBoxName = b"__mbox_handle_clone_box"

// `__mbox_handle_destruct(handleBox)` — the destructor every handle box is minted with. The BOX owns one
// share of the mailbox's `handles` and `refs`, not each reference to it, so a handle is retained and
// dropped by the plain box incref and decref, and only the box's last reference steps the pair. Exported
// because `Parser.emitServiceSpawn` mints the spawned handle's box with it.
export let MboxHandleDestructName = b"__mbox_handle_destruct"

// `__mbox_service_exit(mbox)` — the loop's last act. Exported because `ServiceLoop` emits the call as the
// tail of every synthesized `<T>.__loop`.
export let MboxServiceExitName = b"__mbox_service_exit"

export let MboxReplyRefusedName = b"__mbox_reply_refused"

export let MboxUnknownTagName = b"__mbox_unknown_tag"

let MboxRefusedReplyFlag = ErrorFlagOrdinalBias

// ⭐⭐ **INSTALL THE MAILBOX RUNTIME — behind `usesGt`, at its CALL SITE, exactly as `installSchedRuntime`
// is.** There is no program that wants a mailbox without the green-thread substrate under it: `__svc_spawn`
// calls `__gt_spawn_green` and every wake goes through `__gt_ready_locked`. And there is no bit of its
// own to gate it with, for `SlabRuntime.SlabScavengeName`'s stated reason — these functions gate nothing
// (no import, no `.data` slot, no per-allocation maintenance), and `DeadFunctionElimination` drops them all
// from every program that never spawns a service, because the only edge into them is the `funcAddr`/`call`
// pair `LowerMaxonToStd.lowerServiceSpawn` emits.

export function installMailboxRuntime(module StdModule, requestStagingBytes ByteOffset)
	buildSvcSpawn(module)
	buildMboxStaging(module, bytes: requestStagingBytes)
	buildMboxSend(module)
	buildMboxSendQueue(module)
	buildMboxRecv(module)
	buildMboxRecvTake(module)
	buildMboxClose(module)
	buildMboxSendAbandon(module)
	buildMboxHandleCloneBox(module)
	buildMboxHandleDestruct(module)
	buildMboxServiceExit(module)
	buildMboxReplyRefused(module)
	buildMboxUnknownTag(module)
	buildMboxInterfaceCloneBox(module)
	buildMboxInterfaceSend(module)
end 'installMailboxRuntime'

let MboxInterfaceRuntimePrefix = b"__mbox_iface_"
export let MboxInterfaceCloneBoxName = b"__mbox_iface_clone_box"
export let MboxInterfaceSendName = b"__mbox_iface_send"

let MboxInterfaceConversionPrefix = b"__mbox_iface_from."
let MboxInterfaceStubPrefix = b"__mbox_iface_stub."
let MboxInterfaceTablePrefix = b"__mbox_iface_table."
let MboxInterfaceSlotBytes = 8

export function isInterfaceHandleRuntimeCallee(callee ByteArray) returns bool
	return bytesStartWith(callee, prefix: MboxInterfaceRuntimePrefix)
end 'isInterfaceHandleRuntimeCallee'

export function isInterfaceHandleConversionCallee(callee ByteArray) returns bool
	return bytesStartWith(callee, prefix: MboxInterfaceConversionPrefix)
end 'isInterfaceHandleConversionCallee'

export function interfaceHandleConversionName(serviceTypeName ByteArray, interfaceName ByteArray) returns ByteArray
	return "{String.from(MboxInterfaceConversionPrefix)}{String.from(serviceTypeName)}.{String.from(interfaceName)}".toByteArray()
end 'interfaceHandleConversionName'

function interfaceHandleStubName(serviceTypeName ByteArray, interfaceName ByteArray, slot CaseIndex) returns ByteArray
	return "{String.from(MboxInterfaceStubPrefix)}{String.from(serviceTypeName)}.{String.from(interfaceName)}.{slot}".toByteArray()
end 'interfaceHandleStubName'

function interfaceHandleTableLabel(serviceTypeName ByteArray, interfaceName ByteArray) returns String
	return "{String.from(MboxInterfaceTablePrefix)}{String.from(serviceTypeName)}.{String.from(interfaceName)}"
end 'interfaceHandleTableLabel'

export function interfaceSendSlotOffset(slot CaseIndex) returns FullRangeInt
	return (slot as FullRangeInt) * MboxInterfaceSlotBytes
end 'interfaceSendSlotOffset'

function buildMboxInterfaceCloneBox(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxInterfaceCloneBoxName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let handleBox = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	let table = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: InterfaceHandleTableOffset, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(emitInterfaceHandleBox(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, table: table, ids: ids)))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxInterfaceCloneBox'

function emitInterfaceHandleBox(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, table ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	_ = emitMboxSharesStep(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, delta: MboxShareUnit, ids: ids)
	return emitInterfaceHandleBoxHolding(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, table: table, ids: ids)
end 'emitInterfaceHandleBox'

module function emitInterfaceHandleBoxHolding(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, table ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	let box = emitHandleBoxHolding(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, boxBytes: InterfaceHandleBoxSize, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: box, offset: InterfaceHandleTableOffset, value: table)
	return box
end 'emitInterfaceHandleBoxHolding'

// Every caller takes the mailbox share first (`emitMboxSharesStep` by `MboxShareUnit`): the
// destructor stamped here gives one back, so a box minted without it closes and frees the mailbox
// under a live handle.
function emitHandleBoxHolding(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, boxBytes FullRangeInt, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	let size = emitConst(module, block: block, value: boxBytes, ids: ids)
	let destructor = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(block, op: StdOp.funcAddr(destructor, funcName: MboxHandleDestructName))
	let box = ids.mint()
	emitMmAllocCall(module, block: block, result: box, size: size, destructor: destructor, tag: mmTagIndex(MmTag.Untagged), ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: box, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, value: mbox)
	return box
end 'emitHandleBoxHolding'

function buildMboxInterfaceSend(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxInterfaceSendName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 5, paramTypes: fiveI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(5)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 5)
	let handleBox = 0
	let slotOffset = 1
	let request = 2
	let bytes = 3
	let timeoutMs = 4

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	let table = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: InterfaceHandleTableOffset, ids: ids)
	let stub = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: emitBin(module, block: entry, a: table, b: slotOffset, opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids), offset: 0, ids: ids)
	let status = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.callIndirect(status, calleeReg: stub, resultType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), argFloatMask: 0, args: fourArgs(mbox, second: request, third: bytes, fourth: timeoutMs)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(status))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxInterfaceSend'

// Every interface with a handle, not only the service's own `conformsTo`: a handle widens to an interface
// its service reaches through `extends` (`ProgramSignatures.serviceHandleWidensTo`), and that conversion is
// called too.
export function installInterfaceHandleConversions(module StdModule, globalData GlobalDataTable, usage RuntimeUsage, signatures ProgramSignatures)
	if usage.neededInterfaceConversions.count() == 0 'noConversion'
		return
	end 'noConversion'

	var built = 0 as Count

	for serviceTypeName in serviceCompanionRoster(signatures) 'eachService'
		for interfaceName in signatures.interfacesWithHandles() 'eachInterfaceHandle'
			if usage.neededInterfaceConversions.contains(interfaceHandleConversionName(serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName)) 'thisPairIsConverted'
				buildInterfaceHandleConversion(module, globalData: globalData, signatures: signatures, serviceTypeName: serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName)
				built = built + 1
			end 'thisPairIsConverted'
		end 'eachInterfaceHandle'
	end 'eachService'

	if built != usage.neededInterfaceConversions.count() 'aConversionOfADeadService'
		panic("installInterfaceHandleConversions: {usage.neededInterfaceConversions.count()} conversion(s) are called and {built} were built — a reached body converts the handle of a service that is not on the companion roster, the set `ServiceCompanions.interfaceServiceImplementers` vets")
	end 'aConversionOfADeadService'
end 'installInterfaceHandleConversions'

function buildInterfaceHandleConversion(module StdModule, globalData GlobalDataTable, signatures ProgramSignatures, serviceTypeName ByteArray, interfaceName ByteArray)
	let interfaceRequest = requireServiceRequestLayout(signatures, typeName: interfaceName)
	let serviceRequest = requireServiceRequestLayout(signatures, typeName: serviceTypeName)
	let label = interfaceHandleTableLabel(serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName)
	var blob = ByteArray.create()
	blob.growFilled(interfaceSendSlotOffset(interfaceRequest.caseCount()) as ElementIndex, value: 0)
	_ = globalData.registerRdataConstantLabeled(label, bytes: blob, kind: RdataPayloadKind.witnessTable)

	for slot in 0 upto interfaceRequest.caseCount() 'eachSlot'
		let serviceCase = try serviceRequest.indexOfCase(interfaceRequest.caseNameAt(slot)) otherwise panic("buildInterfaceHandleConversion: `{String.from(serviceTypeName)}` has no message `{String.from(interfaceRequest.caseNameAt(slot))}` of `{String.from(interfaceName)}` — conformance requires every requirement, and a message is an exported instance method")

		let stubName = interfaceHandleStubName(serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName, slot: slot)
		buildInterfaceSendStub(module, name: stubName, serviceTag: serviceRequest.tagOfIndex(serviceCase), interfaceBytes: interfaceRequest.boxSizeBytes(), slotBytes: serviceRequest.boxSizeBytes())
		globalData.recordFuncAbs64InRdata(stubName, rdataLabel: label, offsetInLabel: interfaceSendSlotOffset(slot) as ByteOffset)
	end 'eachSlot'

	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(interfaceHandleConversionName(serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName), returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)
	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let serviceHandle = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: serviceHandle, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	let table = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.rdataAddr(table, label: globalData.labelBytesOf(label)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(emitInterfaceHandleBox(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, table: table, ids: ids)))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildInterfaceHandleConversion'

function buildInterfaceSendStub(module StdModule, name ByteArray, serviceTag FullRangeInt, interfaceBytes ByteOffset, slotBytes ByteOffset)
	if interfaceBytes > slotBytes 'widerThanTheSlot'
		panic("buildInterfaceSendStub: `{String.from(name)}` copies {interfaceBytes} byte(s) of an interface request into a ring slot of {slotBytes} — an interface request union holds only the requirements an implementer declares as messages, so the concrete service's union must be at least as wide, and this pair breaks that")
	end 'widerThanTheSlot'

	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(name, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 4, paramTypes: fourI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(4)
	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 4)
	let mbox = 0
	let request = 1
	let bytes = 2
	let timeoutMs = 3

	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: request, offset: UnionTagOffset, value: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: serviceTag, ids: ids))
	let status = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(status, callee: MboxSendName, args: fourArgs(mbox, second: request, third: bytes, fourth: timeoutMs)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(status))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildInterfaceSendStub'

function emitMboxLockEnter(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	emitLockEnterAt(module, block: block, lock: emitFieldAddr(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffLock, ids: ids), kind: RuntimeLockKind.exclusive, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxLockEnter'

function emitMboxLockLeave(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	emitLockLeaveAt(module, block: block, lock: emitFieldAddr(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffLock, ids: ids), kind: RuntimeLockKind.exclusive, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxLockLeave'

function emitMboxBranchOnParkedReceiver(module StdModule, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, noReceiver IrBlock, handoff IrBlock, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	let parked = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffParkedGt, ids: ids)
	let noneParked = emitConst(module, block: cur, value: 0, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompareValues(module, block: cur, a: parked, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, b: noneParked, whenTrue: noReceiver, whenFalse: handoff, ids: ids)
	return parked
end 'emitMboxBranchOnParkedReceiver'

function emitMboxWakeParked(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, parked ValueId, handed ValueId, cont IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	emitStoreField(module, block: cur, record: parked, offset: GtOffParkArg, value: handed)
	emitStoreField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffParkedGt, value: emitConst(module, block: cur, value: 0, ids: ids))
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: cur, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitGtReadyParkedService(module, func: func, cur: cur, service: parked, cont: cont, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxWakeParked'

function emitMboxSendRoot(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	return emitBin(module, block: block, a: mbox, b: emitConst(module, block: block, value: MboxSendRootBias, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxSendRoot'

function emitMboxSendAppend(module StdModule, block IrBlock, root ValueId, sender ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	let tail = emitLoadField(module, block: block, record: root, offset: GtOffSendPrev, ids: ids)

	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: sender, offset: GtOffSendNext, value: root)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: sender, offset: GtOffSendPrev, value: tail)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: tail, offset: GtOffSendNext, value: sender)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: root, offset: GtOffSendPrev, value: sender)
end 'emitMboxSendAppend'

function emitMboxSendUnlink(module StdModule, block IrBlock, sender ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	let before = emitLoadField(module, block: block, record: sender, offset: GtOffSendPrev, ids: ids)
	let after = emitLoadField(module, block: block, record: sender, offset: GtOffSendNext, ids: ids)
	let unlinked = emitConst(module, block: block, value: 0, ids: ids)

	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: before, offset: GtOffSendNext, value: after)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: after, offset: GtOffSendPrev, value: before)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: sender, offset: GtOffSendNext, value: unlinked)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: sender, offset: GtOffSendPrev, value: unlinked)
end 'emitMboxSendUnlink'

// The CAS from `pending` is the one claim on a waiting sender: of a receive, a close, its timer and
// an abandon, only the winner readies it, and a loser leaves it alone. Two readies of one thread
// would run it on two machines at once.
export function emitMboxClaimSender(module StdModule, block IrBlock, sender ValueId, outcome MboxSendWake, lost IrBlock, won IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	let claim = emitCasField(module, block: block, record: sender, offset: GtOffSendOutcome as ByteOffset, expected: emitConst(module, block: block, value: MboxSendWake.pending.rawValue, ids: ids), replacement: emitConst(module, block: block, value: outcome.rawValue, ids: ids), ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCasLost(module, block: block, result: claim, lost: lost, won: won, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxClaimSender'

function emitMboxClaimFrontSender(module StdModule, func IrFunction, scan IrBlock, root ValueId, outcome MboxSendWake, empty IrBlock, won IrBlock, carried ValueIdArray, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	var claim = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendfrontclaim", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var skip = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendfrontskip", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	let front = emitMboxBranchOnSenders(module, block: scan, root: root, waiting: claim, none: empty, ids: ids)

	emitMboxClaimSender(module, block: claim, sender: front, outcome: outcome, lost: skip, won: won, ids: ids)

	emitMboxSendUnlink(module, block: skip, sender: front, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(skip, op: StdOp.branch(scan.id))

	if carried.count() > 0 'carriesValues'
		skip.branchEdges.push(BranchEdge.create(scan.id, argIds: carried))
	end 'carriesValues'

	return front
end 'emitMboxClaimFrontSender'

// The `TimerTagSend` entry goes before the ready, in the same `__sched_lock` hold: a readied sender
// may park again at once, and a stale entry would claim that park `timedOut`.
function emitMboxReadyClaimedSender(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, sender ValueId, cont IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	var disarm = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwakedisarm", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var ready = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwakeready", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitSchedLockEnter(module, block: cur, ids: ids)
	let deadline = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: sender, offset: GtOffSendDeadline, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: cur, value: deadline, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: GtDeadlineMaxNs, whenTrue: ready, whenFalse: disarm, ids: ids)

	emitGtTimerStoreRemove(module, func: func, ids: ids, startBlock: disarm, gt: sender, tag: emitConst(module, block: disarm, value: TimerTagSend, ids: ids), found: ready, missing: ready)

	let debt = emitGtReady(module, block: ready, gt: sender, gate: GtReadyGate.fromWaiting, ids: ids)
	emitSchedLockLeave(module, block: ready, ids: ids)
	emitBranchCarrying(module, from: ready, to: cont, value: debt)
end 'emitMboxReadyClaimedSender'

function emitMboxHandOffClaimedSender(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, sender ValueId, cont IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	emitMboxSendUnlink(module, block: cur, sender: sender, ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: cur, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitMboxReadyClaimedSender(module, func: func, cur: cur, sender: sender, cont: cont, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxHandOffClaimedSender'

function emitMboxSlotAddr(module StdModule, block IrBlock, ring ValueId, index ValueId, slotBytes ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	return emitBin(module, block: block, a: ring, b: emitBin(module, block: block, a: index, b: slotBytes, opcode: StdBinOpcode.mul, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxSlotAddr'

function emitMboxInitialSlots(module StdModule, block IrBlock, capacity ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	var slots = emitConst(module, block: block, value: 1, ids: ids)
	var reach = 1 as FullRangeInt

	while reach < MboxInitialSlots 'eachDoubling'
		let wider = emitCmp(module, block: block, a: capacity, b: slots, pred: StdCmpPred.gt, ids: ids)
		slots = emitBin(module, block: block, a: slots, b: wider, opcode: StdBinOpcode.shl, ids: ids)
		reach = reach * MboxSlotGrowth
	end 'eachDoubling'

	return slots
end 'emitMboxInitialSlots'

function emitMboxInboxAddr(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	return emitFieldAddr(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffInbox, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxInboxAddr'

function emitMboxBranchOnFull(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, inboxHolds bool, full IrBlock, room IrBlock, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	let ringCount = emitLoadField(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCount, ids: ids)
	var queued = ringCount

	if inboxHolds 'inboxHolds'
		queued = emitBin(module, block: block, a: ringCount, b: emitConst(module, block: block, value: MboxInboxHeldMessages, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids)
	end 'inboxHolds'

	let capacity = emitLoadField(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCapacity, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompareValues(module, block: block, a: queued, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, b: capacity, whenTrue: full, whenFalse: room, ids: ids)

	return ringCount
end 'emitMboxBranchOnFull'

function emitMboxInboxFirst(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, msg ValueId, byteCount ValueId, done IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	var filled = emitMboxFillInbox(module, func: func, cur: cur, mbox: mbox, msg: msg, byteCount: byteCount, ids: ids)
	emitMboxSetReceiver(module, block: filled, mbox: mbox, state: MboxReceiverState.inboxQueued, ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: filled, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(filled, op: StdOp.branch(done.id))
end 'emitMboxInboxFirst'

function emitMboxBranchOnRingRoom(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ringCount ValueId, room IrBlock, noRoom IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	var haveRing = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxhavering", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	let ring = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: cur, value: ring, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: noRoom, whenFalse: haveRing, ids: ids)

	let ringSlots = emitLoadField(module, block: haveRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompareValues(module, block: haveRing, a: ringCount, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, b: ringSlots, whenTrue: noRoom, whenFalse: room, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxBranchOnRingRoom'

function emitMboxRingPlace(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ringCount ValueId, msg ValueId, byteCount ValueId, done IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	emitStoreField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCount, value: emitBin(module, block: cur, a: ringCount, b: emitConst(module, block: cur, value: 1, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids))
	var stored = emitMboxRingStoreTail(module, func: func, cur: cur, mbox: mbox, ringCount: ringCount, msg: msg, byteCount: byteCount, ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: stored, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(stored, op: StdOp.branch(done.id))
end 'emitMboxRingPlace'

function emitMboxBranchOnSenders(module StdModule, block IrBlock, root ValueId, waiting IrBlock, none IrBlock, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	let front = emitLoadField(module, block: block, record: root, offset: GtOffSendNext, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompareValues(module, block: block, a: front, pred: StdCmpPred.ne, b: root, whenTrue: waiting, whenFalse: none, ids: ids)

	return front
end 'emitMboxBranchOnSenders'

function emitMboxRingPop(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, remaining ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns IrBlock
	let ring = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, ids: ids)
	let head = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, ids: ids)
	let ringSlots = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, ids: ids)
	let slotBytes = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSlotBytes, ids: ids)
	let source = emitMboxSlotAddr(module, block: cur, ring: ring, index: head, slotBytes: slotBytes, ids: ids)
	let slotMask = emitBin(module, block: cur, a: ringSlots, b: emitConst(module, block: cur, value: 1, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.sub, ids: ids)
	let newHead = emitBin(module, block: cur, a: emitBin(module, block: cur, a: head, b: emitConst(module, block: cur, value: 1, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids), b: slotMask, opcode: StdBinOpcode.bitAnd, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, value: newHead)
	emitStoreField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCount, value: remaining)

	return emitForwardCopy(module, func: func, cur: cur, dest: emitMboxInboxAddr(module, block: cur, mbox: mbox, ids: ids), src: source, byteCount: slotBytes, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxRingPop'

function emitMboxSetReceiver(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, state MboxReceiverState, ids ValueMinter)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffReceiver, value: emitConst(module, block: block, value: state.rawValue, ids: ids))
end 'emitMboxSetReceiver'

function emitMboxDispatchReceiverState(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, receiver ValueId, started IrBlock, fresh IrBlock, inboxQueued IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	var notStarted = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxstatenotstarted", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var notFresh = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxstatenotfresh", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: cur, value: receiver, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxReceiverState.started.rawValue, whenTrue: started, whenFalse: notStarted, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: notStarted, value: receiver, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxReceiverState.fresh.rawValue, whenTrue: fresh, whenFalse: notFresh, ids: ids)

	emitMboxBranchOnInboxQueued(module, func: func, cur: notFresh, receiver: receiver, inboxQueued: inboxQueued, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxDispatchReceiverState'

function emitMboxDispatchQueuedState(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, receiver ValueId, started IrBlock, inboxQueued IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	var notStarted = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxstatenotstarted", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: cur, value: receiver, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxReceiverState.started.rawValue, whenTrue: started, whenFalse: notStarted, ids: ids)

	emitMboxBranchOnInboxQueued(module, func: func, cur: notStarted, receiver: receiver, inboxQueued: inboxQueued, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxDispatchQueuedState'

function emitMboxBranchOnInboxQueued(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, receiver ValueId, inboxQueued IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	var outOfDomain = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxstateoutofdomain", heat: BlockHeat.cold)

	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: cur, value: receiver, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxReceiverState.inboxQueued.rawValue, whenTrue: inboxQueued, whenFalse: outOfDomain, ids: ids)

	emitRuntimeFatal(module, func: func, block: outOfDomain, fatal: RuntimeFatal.mailboxReceiverStateOutOfDomain, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxBranchOnInboxQueued'

function emitMboxFillInbox(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, msg ValueId, byteCount ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns IrBlock
	return emitForwardCopy(module, func: func, cur: cur, dest: emitMboxInboxAddr(module, block: cur, mbox: mbox, ids: ids), src: msg, byteCount: byteCount, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxFillInbox'

function emitMboxRingReserve(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ringCount ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns IrBlock
	var needsRing = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxneedsring", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var seedRing = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxseedring", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var growRing = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxgrowring", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var place = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxplace", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitMboxBranchOnRingRoom(module, func: func, cur: cur, mbox: mbox, ringCount: ringCount, room: place, noRoom: needsRing, ids: ids)

	let ring = emitLoadField(module, block: needsRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: needsRing, value: ring, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: seedRing, whenFalse: growRing, ids: ids)

	let initialSlots = emitMboxInitialSlots(module, block: seedRing, capacity: emitLoadField(module, block: seedRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCapacity, ids: ids), ids: ids)
	let seeded = emitMboxRingAlloc(module, block: seedRing, slotBytes: emitLoadField(module, block: seedRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSlotBytes, ids: ids), slots: initialSlots, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: seedRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, value: seeded)
	emitStoreField(module, block: seedRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, value: initialSlots)
	module.setTerminator(seedRing, op: StdOp.branch(place.id))

	let ringSlots = emitLoadField(module, block: growRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, ids: ids)
	let oldHead = emitLoadField(module, block: growRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, ids: ids)
	let growSlotBytes = emitLoadField(module, block: growRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSlotBytes, ids: ids)
	let grownSlots = emitBin(module, block: growRing, a: ringSlots, b: emitConst(module, block: growRing, value: MboxSlotGrowth, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.mul, ids: ids)
	let grown = emitMboxRingAlloc(module, block: growRing, slotBytes: growSlotBytes, slots: grownSlots, ids: ids)
	let tailRunBytes = emitBin(module, block: growRing, a: emitBin(module, block: growRing, a: ringSlots, b: oldHead, opcode: StdBinOpcode.sub, ids: ids), b: growSlotBytes, opcode: StdBinOpcode.mul, ids: ids)
	let oldRing = emitLoadField(module, block: growRing, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, ids: ids)
	var copiedTailRun = emitForwardCopy(module, func: func, cur: growRing, dest: grown, src: emitMboxSlotAddr(module, block: growRing, ring: oldRing, index: oldHead, slotBytes: growSlotBytes, ids: ids), byteCount: tailRunBytes, ids: ids)
	let headRunBytes = emitBin(module, block: copiedTailRun, a: oldHead, b: growSlotBytes, opcode: StdBinOpcode.mul, ids: ids)
	var copiedHeadRun = emitForwardCopy(module, func: func, cur: copiedTailRun, dest: emitBin(module, block: copiedTailRun, a: grown, b: tailRunBytes, opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids), src: oldRing, byteCount: headRunBytes, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: copiedHeadRun, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, value: grown)
	emitStoreField(module, block: copiedHeadRun, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, value: grownSlots)
	emitStoreField(module, block: copiedHeadRun, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, value: emitConst(module, block: copiedHeadRun, value: MboxRingHeadReset, ids: ids))
	emitSlabScaffoldFree(module, block: copiedHeadRun, ptr: oldRing, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(copiedHeadRun, op: StdOp.branch(place.id))

	return place
end 'emitMboxRingReserve'

function emitMboxRingStoreTail(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ringCount ValueId, msg ValueId, byteCount ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns IrBlock
	let ring = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, ids: ids)
	let ringSlots = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, ids: ids)
	let head = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, ids: ids)
	let slotBytes = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSlotBytes, ids: ids)
	let slotMask = emitBin(module, block: cur, a: ringSlots, b: emitConst(module, block: cur, value: 1, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.sub, ids: ids)
	let tailIndex = emitBin(module, block: cur, a: emitBin(module, block: cur, a: head, b: ringCount, opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids), b: slotMask, opcode: StdBinOpcode.bitAnd, ids: ids)

	return emitForwardCopy(module, func: func, cur: cur, dest: emitMboxSlotAddr(module, block: cur, ring: ring, index: tailIndex, slotBytes: slotBytes, ids: ids), src: msg, byteCount: byteCount, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxRingStoreTail'

function emitMboxAdmitClaimedSender(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, sender ValueId, ringCount ValueId, cont IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	let staging = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: sender, offset: GtOffStaging, ids: ids)
	let slotBytes = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSlotBytes, ids: ids)
	var placed = emitMboxRingStoreTail(module, func: func, cur: cur, mbox: mbox, ringCount: ringCount, msg: staging, byteCount: slotBytes, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: placed, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCount, value: emitBin(module, block: placed, a: ringCount, b: emitConst(module, block: placed, value: 1, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids))
	emitMboxHandOffClaimedSender(module, func: func, cur: placed, mbox: mbox, sender: sender, cont: cont, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxAdmitClaimedSender'

// The ring takes the scaffold door (`SlabRuntime.SlabScaffoldAllocName`, for its reason) where the
// mailbox region beside it is counted: the region is cut once per spawn, while whether a ring is
// cut, grown or shrunk follows the schedule.
function emitMboxRingAlloc(module StdModule, block IrBlock, slotBytes ValueId, slots ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	let ring = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(block, op: StdOp.call(ring, callee: SlabScaffoldAllocName, args: argsOf(emitBin(module, block: block, a: slots, b: slotBytes, opcode: StdBinOpcode.mul, ids: ids))))
	return ring
end 'emitMboxRingAlloc'

function emitMboxFreeRegion(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns IrBlock
	var freeRing = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxfreering", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var freeRegion = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxfreeregion", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	let ring = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: cur, value: ring, pred: StdCmpPred.ne, against: 0, whenTrue: freeRing, whenFalse: freeRegion, ids: ids)

	emitSlabScaffoldFree(module, block: freeRing, ptr: ring, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(freeRing, op: StdOp.branch(freeRegion.id))

	emitSlabFree(module, block: freeRegion, ptr: mbox, ids: ids)

	return freeRegion
end 'emitMboxFreeRegion'

// Answers the PRIOR word. "Was I the last" is read off it and never off a re-load, which a
// concurrent drop could already have moved.
module function emitMboxSharesStep(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, delta FullRangeInt, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	return emitFieldAccumulate(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffShares, delta: emitConst(module, block: block, value: delta, ids: ids), multiM: true, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxSharesStep'

// `__svc_spawn(loopPtr, state, slotBytes, capacity) -> mbox`. See `SvcSpawnName`.
function buildSvcSpawn(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(SvcSpawnName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 4, paramTypes: fourI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(4)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 4)
	let loopPtr = 0
	let state = 1
	let slotBytes = 2
	let capacity = 3

	// `__slab_alloc` ZEROES, so the ring, its indices, parkedGt, closed and receiver
	// (`MboxReceiverState.fresh`) are already their correct initial state and only the words a
	// zero would be wrong for are stored.
	let mboxBytes = emitBin(module, block: entry, a: slotBytes, b: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxHeaderBytes, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids)
	let mbox = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(mbox, callee: SlabAllocName, args: argsOf(mboxBytes)))
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSlotBytes, value: slotBytes)
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffShares, value: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxInitialShares, ids: ids))
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCapacity, value: capacity)
	let sendRoot = emitMboxSendRoot(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSendNext, value: sendRoot)
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSendPrev, value: sendRoot)

	// ⭐⭐ **`__gt_spawn_green`, NOT `__gt_spawn` — a SERVICE IS A GREEN THREAD AND NOT A COROUTINE.** The two
	// bodies differ in one store (a coroutine copies its spawner's owner; a green thread is stamped with
	// itself), and that store is what makes this thread the head of a strand of its own, whose token goes to a
	// P's RING, rather than a member of its spawner's strand. A coroutine here would run only where its
	// spawner's work runs, which is exactly the property a service must not have.
	let gt = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(gt, callee: GtSpawnGreenName, args: argsOf(loopPtr)))
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: gt, offset: GtOffArgInline as ByteOffset, value: state)
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: gt, offset: (GtOffArgInline + GtArgSlotBytes) as ByteOffset, value: mbox)
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: GtReadyName, args: argsOf(gt)))

	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(mbox))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildSvcSpawn'

// `__mbox_staging() -> record`. See `MboxStagingName`.
function buildMboxStaging(module StdModule, bytes ByteOffset)
	if (bytes as FullRangeInt) > SchedArenaChunkBytes 'largerThanAChunk'
		panic("buildMboxStaging: the largest request union is {bytes} byte(s), past the {SchedArenaChunkBytes}-byte scheduler-arena chunk a carve cannot span")
	end 'largerThanAChunk'

	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxStagingName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 0, paramTypes: StdTypeArray.create())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(0)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var carve = module.addBlock(func, label: b"stagingcarve", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var have = module.addBlock(func, label: b"staginghave", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	let selfGt = emitLoadCurrentGt(module, block: entry, ids: ids)
	let staging = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffStaging as ByteOffset, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: entry, value: staging, pred: StdCmpPred.ne, against: 0, whenTrue: have, whenFalse: carve, ids: ids)

	module.setTerminator(have, op: StdOp.ret(staging))

	emitLockWordEnter(module, block: carve, label: GtFreeLockLabel, kind: RuntimeLockKind.recursive, ids: ids)
	let carved = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(carve, op: StdOp.call(carved, callee: SchedArenaCarveName, args: argsOf(emitConst(module, block: carve, value: bytes as FullRangeInt, ids: ids))))
	emitLockWordLeave(module, block: carve, label: GtFreeLockLabel, kind: RuntimeLockKind.recursive, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: carve, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffStaging as ByteOffset, value: carved)
	module.setTerminator(carve, op: StdOp.ret(carved))

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxStaging'

// `__mbox_send(mbox, msg, bytes, timeoutMs)`. See `MboxSendName`.
function buildMboxSend(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxSendName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 4, paramTypes: fourI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(4)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var attempt = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendtry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var refuseClosed = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendclosed", heat: BlockHeat.cold)
	var route = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendroute", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var handoff = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendhandoff", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var firstCheck = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendfirstcheck", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var inboxFirst = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendinboxfirst", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var append = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendappend", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var ringRoom = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendringroom", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var fitted = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendfitted", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var queueing = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendqueueing", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var doneBlock = module.addBlock(func, label: b"senddone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 4)
	let mbox = 0
	let msg = 1
	let bytes = 2
	let timeoutMs = 3

	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.branch(attempt.id))

	let closed = emitLoadField(module, block: attempt, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffClosed, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: attempt, value: closed, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: route, whenFalse: refuseClosed, ids: ids)

	emitMboxRefuse(module, block: refuseClosed, mbox: mbox, status: MboxSendStatus.stopped, ids: ids)

	// Handing past the ring keeps FIFO order only because a receiver parks on an empty, open mailbox
	// alone, so a non-zero `parkedGt` under the lock means nothing is queued ahead of this request.
	let parked = emitMboxBranchOnParkedReceiver(module, cur: route, mbox: mbox, noReceiver: firstCheck, handoff: handoff, ids: ids)

	var delivered = emitMboxFillInbox(module, func: func, cur: handoff, mbox: mbox, msg: msg, byteCount: bytes, ids: ids)
	emitMboxWakeParked(module, func: func, cur: delivered, mbox: mbox, parked: parked, handed: emitConst(module, block: delivered, value: MboxHandedMessage, ids: ids), cont: doneBlock, ids: ids)

	let receiver = emitLoadField(module, block: firstCheck, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffReceiver, ids: ids)
	emitMboxDispatchReceiverState(module, func: func, cur: firstCheck, receiver: receiver, started: append, fresh: inboxFirst, inboxQueued: queueing, ids: ids)

	emitMboxInboxFirst(module, func: func, cur: inboxFirst, mbox: mbox, msg: msg, byteCount: bytes, done: doneBlock, ids: ids)

	let ringCount = emitMboxBranchOnFull(module, block: append, mbox: mbox, inboxHolds: false, full: queueing, room: ringRoom, ids: ids)

	emitMboxBranchOnRingRoom(module, func: func, cur: ringRoom, mbox: mbox, ringCount: ringCount, room: fitted, noRoom: queueing, ids: ids)

	emitMboxRingPlace(module, func: func, cur: fitted, mbox: mbox, ringCount: ringCount, msg: msg, byteCount: bytes, done: doneBlock, ids: ids)

	let status = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(queueing, op: StdOp.call(status, callee: MboxSendQueueName, args: fourArgs(mbox, second: msg, third: bytes, fourth: timeoutMs)))
	module.setTerminator(queueing, op: StdOp.ret(status))

	module.setTerminator(doneBlock, op: StdOp.ret(emitConst(module, block: doneBlock, value: MboxSendStatus.delivered.rawValue, ids: ids)))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxSend'

// `__mbox_send_queue(mbox, msg, bytes, timeoutMs)`. See `MboxSendQueueName`.
function buildMboxSendQueue(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxSendQueueName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 4, paramTypes: fourI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(4)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var append = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendappend", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var appendBehindInbox = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendappendbehindinbox", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var roomGate = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendroomgate", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var refuseFull = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendfull", heat: BlockHeat.cold)
	var waitCheck = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwaitcheck", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var waitGate = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwaitgate", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var stagingMismatch = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendstagingmismatch", heat: BlockHeat.cold)
	var enqueue = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendenqueue", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var deadlined = module.addBlock(func, label: b"senddeadlined", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var woken = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwoken", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var wakeLocked = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwakelocked", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var timedOut = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendtimedout", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var wakeUnlocked = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwakeunlocked", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var wakeFailed = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwakefailed", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var wakeStopped = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwakestopped", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var wakeNotStopped = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwakenotstopped", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var wakeUnexpected = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendwakeunexpected", heat: BlockHeat.cold)
	var queue = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendqueue", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var doneBlock = module.addBlock(func, label: b"senddone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 4)
	let mbox = 0
	let msg = 1
	let bytes = 2
	let timeoutMs = 3

	let receiver = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffReceiver, ids: ids)
	emitMboxDispatchQueuedState(module, func: func, cur: entry, receiver: receiver, started: append, inboxQueued: appendBehindInbox, ids: ids)

	_ = emitMboxBranchOnFull(module, block: append, mbox: mbox, inboxHolds: false, full: roomGate, room: queue, ids: ids)
	_ = emitMboxBranchOnFull(module, block: appendBehindInbox, mbox: mbox, inboxHolds: true, full: roomGate, room: queue, ids: ids)

	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: roomGate, value: timeoutMs, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: refuseFull, whenFalse: waitCheck, ids: ids)

	emitMboxRefuse(module, block: refuseFull, mbox: mbox, status: MboxSendStatus.full, ids: ids)

	// A scheduler context has no green thread to park, and a renounced coroutine is never awaited, so
	// both answer `full` at once. No drop can land between this read and the park commit: a dropper
	// runs on the machine holding this sender's strand, which is busy running the sender
	// (`__gt_promise_drop` checks it).
	let selfGt = emitLoadCurrentGt(module, block: waitCheck, ids: ids)
	let stackBase = emitLoadField(module, block: waitCheck, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffStackBase, ids: ids)
	let onGreenStack = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: waitCheck, value: stackBase, pred: StdCmpPred.ne, against: 0, ids: ids)
	let renounced = emitLoadField(module, block: waitCheck, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffRenounced, ids: ids)
	let promiseHeld = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: waitCheck, value: renounced, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: GtPromiseHeld, ids: ids)
	let mayWait = emitBin(module, block: waitCheck, a: onGreenStack, b: promiseHeld, opcode: StdBinOpcode.bitAnd, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(waitCheck, op: StdOp.condBranch(mayWait, thenBlockId: waitGate.id, elseBlockId: refuseFull.id))

	let staging = emitLoadField(module, block: waitGate, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffStaging, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompareValues(module, block: waitGate, a: msg, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, b: staging, whenTrue: enqueue, whenFalse: stagingMismatch, ids: ids)

	emitRuntimeAbort(module, func: func, block: stagingMismatch, abort: RuntimeAbort.serviceSendProtocolBroken, ids: ids)

	let sendRoot = emitMboxSendRoot(module, block: enqueue, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: enqueue, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffSendOutcome, value: emitConst(module, block: enqueue, value: MboxSendWake.pending.rawValue, ids: ids))
	let sendDeadline = emitGtDeadlineAfterMs(module, func: func, cur: enqueue, ms: timeoutMs, joined: deadlined, ids: ids)

	emitStoreField(module, block: deadlined, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffSendDeadline, value: sendDeadline)
	emitMboxSendAppend(module, block: deadlined, root: sendRoot, sender: selfGt, ids: ids)

	emitGtPark(module, ids: ids, cur: deadlined, kind: GtParkKind.mailboxSend.rawValue, arg: mbox, cont: woken)

	let wakeOutcome = emitLoadAcquireField(module, block: woken, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffSendOutcome, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: woken, value: wakeOutcome, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxSendWake.delivered.rawValue, whenTrue: doneBlock, whenFalse: wakeFailed, ids: ids)

	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: wakeFailed, value: wakeOutcome, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxSendWake.stopped.rawValue, whenTrue: wakeStopped, whenFalse: wakeNotStopped, ids: ids)
	emitConstReturn(module, block: wakeStopped, value: MboxSendStatus.stopped.rawValue, ids: ids)

	let wasTimedOut = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: wakeNotStopped, value: wakeOutcome, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxSendWake.timedOut.rawValue, ids: ids)
	let wasCancelled = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: wakeNotStopped, value: wakeOutcome, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxSendWake.cancelled.rawValue, ids: ids)
	let wasRefused = emitBin(module, block: wakeNotStopped, a: wasTimedOut, b: wasCancelled, opcode: StdBinOpcode.bitOr, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(wakeNotStopped, op: StdOp.condBranch(wasRefused, thenBlockId: wakeLocked.id, elseBlockId: wakeUnexpected.id))

	// A timer claims without the mailbox lock, so a timed-out sender may still be queued, unless a
	// receive or close that lost the claim unlinked it in passing. It must be off the queue before it
	// returns, or a later pass would unlink a record that has moved on.
	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: wakeLocked, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	let stillQueued = emitLoadField(module, block: wakeLocked, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffSendNext, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: wakeLocked, value: stillQueued, pred: StdCmpPred.ne, against: 0, whenTrue: timedOut, whenFalse: wakeUnlocked, ids: ids)

	emitMboxSendUnlink(module, block: timedOut, sender: selfGt, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(timedOut, op: StdOp.branch(wakeUnlocked.id))

	emitMboxRefuse(module, block: wakeUnlocked, mbox: mbox, status: MboxSendStatus.full, ids: ids)

	emitRuntimeAbort(module, func: func, block: wakeUnexpected, abort: RuntimeAbort.serviceSendProtocolBroken, ids: ids)

	let ringCount = emitLoadField(module, block: queue, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCount, ids: ids)
	var reserved = emitMboxRingReserve(module, func: func, cur: queue, mbox: mbox, ringCount: ringCount, ids: ids)
	emitMboxRingPlace(module, func: func, cur: reserved, mbox: mbox, ringCount: ringCount, msg: msg, byteCount: bytes, done: doneBlock, ids: ids)

	module.setTerminator(doneBlock, op: StdOp.ret(emitConst(module, block: doneBlock, value: MboxSendStatus.delivered.rawValue, ids: ids)))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxSendQueue'

function emitMboxRefuse(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, status MboxSendStatus, ids ValueMinter)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitConstReturn(module, block: block, value: status.rawValue, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxRefuse'

// `__mbox_recv(mbox) -> inbox | 0`. See `MboxRecvName`.
function buildMboxRecv(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxRecvName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var attempt = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvtry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var startFresh = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvstartfresh", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var takeInbox = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvtakeinbox", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var takeInboxAlone = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvtakeinboxalone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var takeInboxContended = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvtakeinboxcontended", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var counted = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvcounted", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var popCheck = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvpopcheck", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var popFit = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvpopfit", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var popNow = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvpopnow", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var takeRing = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvtakering", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var emptyQueue = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvempty", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var drained = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvdrained", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var park = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvpark", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var resumed = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvresumed", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var delivered = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvdelivered", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let mbox = 0
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.branch(attempt.id))

	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: attempt, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	let receiver = emitLoadField(module, block: attempt, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffReceiver, ids: ids)
	emitMboxDispatchReceiverState(module, func: func, cur: attempt, receiver: receiver, started: counted, fresh: startFresh, inboxQueued: takeInbox, ids: ids)

	// Marked before any park: a receiver resumed with a handed message while still `fresh` would
	// let the next send overwrite the inbox it is reading.
	emitMboxSetReceiver(module, block: startFresh, mbox: mbox, state: MboxReceiverState.started, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(startFresh, op: StdOp.branch(counted.id))

	_ = emitMboxBranchOnSenders(module, block: takeInbox, root: emitMboxSendRoot(module, block: takeInbox, mbox: mbox, ids: ids), waiting: takeInboxContended, none: takeInboxAlone, ids: ids)

	emitMboxSetReceiver(module, block: takeInboxAlone, mbox: mbox, state: MboxReceiverState.started, ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: takeInboxAlone, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(takeInboxAlone, op: StdOp.ret(emitMboxInboxAddr(module, block: takeInboxAlone, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)))

	emitMboxTakeCall(module, block: takeInboxContended, mbox: mbox, source: MboxTakeSource.inbox, ids: ids)

	let queued = emitLoadField(module, block: counted, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCount, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: counted, value: queued, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: emptyQueue, whenFalse: popCheck, ids: ids)

	_ = emitMboxBranchOnSenders(module, block: popCheck, root: emitMboxSendRoot(module, block: popCheck, mbox: mbox, ids: ids), waiting: takeRing, none: popFit, ids: ids)

	let ringSlots = emitLoadField(module, block: popFit, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, ids: ids)
	let lastOfGrown = emitBin(module, block: popFit, a: emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: popFit, value: queued, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 1, ids: ids), b: emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: popFit, value: ringSlots, pred: StdCmpPred.gt, against: MboxInitialSlots, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.bitAnd, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(popFit, op: StdOp.condBranch(lastOfGrown, thenBlockId: takeRing.id, elseBlockId: popNow.id))

	var popped = emitMboxRingPop(module, func: func, cur: popNow, mbox: mbox, remaining: emitBin(module, block: popNow, a: queued, b: emitConst(module, block: popNow, value: 1, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.sub, ids: ids), ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: popped, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(popped, op: StdOp.ret(emitMboxInboxAddr(module, block: popped, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)))

	emitMboxTakeCall(module, block: takeRing, mbox: mbox, source: MboxTakeSource.ring, ids: ids)

	// ⭐ **THE `closed` READ IS INSIDE THE SAME CRITICAL SECTION THE COUNT READ WAS**, which is what
	// makes "empty AND closed" one instant rather than two: a close that landed between two separate
	// reads would leave this thread parking on a mailbox nobody will ever send to again.
	let closed = emitLoadField(module, block: emptyQueue, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffClosed, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: emptyQueue, value: closed, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: park, whenFalse: drained, ids: ids)

	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: drained, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitConstReturn(module, block: drained, value: MboxClosedAndDrained, ids: ids)

	// The hold that read "empty and open" stays open through the park (see the file header), so no
	// send or close can land between that read and this registration. On resume, a send has copied its
	// request into the inbox and marked `GtOffParkArg`; a close leaves it empty, and the retry finds
	// the mailbox closed.
	let selfGt = emitLoadCurrentGt(module, block: park, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: park, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffParkedGt, value: selfGt)

	emitGtPark(module, ids: ids, cur: park, kind: GtParkKind.mailbox.rawValue, arg: mbox, cont: resumed)

	let handed = emitLoadField(module, block: resumed, record: selfGt, offset: GtOffParkArg, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: resumed, value: handed, pred: StdCmpPred.ne, against: MboxNoHandedMessage, whenTrue: delivered, whenFalse: attempt, ids: ids)

	module.setTerminator(delivered, op: StdOp.ret(emitMboxInboxAddr(module, block: delivered, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)))

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxRecv'

function emitMboxTakeCall(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, source MboxTakeSource, ids ValueMinter)
	let inbox = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(block, op: StdOp.call(inbox, callee: MboxRecvTakeName, args: twoArgs(mbox, second: emitConst(module, block: block, value: source.rawValue, ids: ids))))
	module.setTerminator(block, op: StdOp.ret(inbox))
end 'emitMboxTakeCall'

// `__mbox_recv_take(mbox, source) -> inbox`. See `MboxRecvTakeName`.
function buildMboxRecvTake(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxRecvTakeName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 2, paramTypes: twoI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(2)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var notInbox = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takenotinbox", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var sourceOutOfDomain = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takesourceoutofdomain", heat: BlockHeat.cold)
	var takeInbox = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takeinbox", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var inboxScan = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takeinboxscan", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var inboxWakeSender = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takeinboxwakesender", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var pop = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takepop", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var shrink = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takeshrink", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var popped = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takepopped", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var noSender = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takenosender", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var senderScan = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takesenderscan", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var wakeSender = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takewakesender", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var senderWoken = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takesenderwoken", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var senderWake = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takesenderwake", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var senderPaid = module.addBlock(func, label: b"takesenderpaid", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 2)
	let mbox = 0
	let source = 1

	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: entry, value: source, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxTakeSource.inbox.rawValue, whenTrue: takeInbox, whenFalse: notInbox, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: notInbox, value: source, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxTakeSource.ring.rawValue, whenTrue: pop, whenFalse: sourceOutOfDomain, ids: ids)

	emitRuntimeFatal(module, func: func, block: sourceOutOfDomain, fatal: RuntimeFatal.mailboxTakeSourceOutOfDomain, ids: ids)

	// Answered whether or not the mailbox has closed, as a ringed message is. The slot of capacity it
	// frees goes to the first waiting sender at once, for the pop's reason (`wakeSender`).
	emitMboxSetReceiver(module, block: takeInbox, mbox: mbox, state: MboxReceiverState.started, ids: ids)
	let ringRemaining = emitLoadField(module, block: takeInbox, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCount, ids: ids)
	let inboxSendRoot = emitMboxSendRoot(module, block: takeInbox, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(takeInbox, op: StdOp.branch(inboxScan.id))

	let inboxSender = emitMboxClaimFrontSender(module, func: func, scan: inboxScan, root: inboxSendRoot, outcome: MboxSendWake.delivered, empty: noSender, won: inboxWakeSender, carried: ValueIdArray.create(), ids: ids)

	var inboxReserved = emitMboxRingReserve(module, func: func, cur: inboxWakeSender, mbox: mbox, ringCount: ringRemaining, ids: ids)
	emitMboxAdmitClaimedSender(module, func: func, cur: inboxReserved, mbox: mbox, sender: inboxSender, ringCount: ringRemaining, cont: senderWoken, ids: ids)

	let queued = emitLoadField(module, block: pop, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffCount, ids: ids)
	let remaining = emitBin(module, block: pop, a: queued, b: emitConst(module, block: pop, value: 1, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.sub, ids: ids)
	var copiedOut = emitMboxRingPop(module, func: func, cur: pop, mbox: mbox, remaining: remaining, ids: ids)
	let sendRoot = emitMboxSendRoot(module, block: copiedOut, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(copiedOut, op: StdOp.branch(senderScan.id))

	let firstSender = emitMboxClaimFrontSender(module, func: func, scan: senderScan, root: sendRoot, outcome: MboxSendWake.delivered, empty: popped, won: wakeSender, carried: ValueIdArray.create(), ids: ids)

	// The slot this pop freed goes to the first sender it claims, at once, so a send arriving later
	// cannot take it ahead of the senders that waited.
	emitMboxAdmitClaimedSender(module, func: func, cur: wakeSender, mbox: mbox, sender: firstSender, ringCount: remaining, cont: senderWoken, ids: ids)

	let nowEmpty = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: popped, value: remaining, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, ids: ids)
	let ringSlots = emitLoadField(module, block: popped, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, ids: ids)
	let grownPast = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: popped, value: ringSlots, pred: StdCmpPred.gt, against: MboxInitialSlots, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(popped, op: StdOp.condBranch(emitBin(module, block: popped, a: nowEmpty, b: grownPast, opcode: StdBinOpcode.bitAnd, ids: ids), thenBlockId: shrink.id, elseBlockId: noSender.id))

	// A grown ring drained empty is replaced by a fresh initial-size one, so a burst's backlog is not
	// held for the mailbox's life.
	let initialSlots = emitConst(module, block: shrink, value: MboxInitialSlots, ids: ids)
	let ring = emitLoadField(module, block: shrink, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, ids: ids)
	let fresh = emitMboxRingAlloc(module, block: shrink, slotBytes: emitLoadField(module, block: shrink, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffSlotBytes, ids: ids), slots: initialSlots, ids: ids)
	emitSlabScaffoldFree(module, block: shrink, ptr: ring, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: shrink, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRing, value: fresh)
	emitStoreField(module, block: shrink, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRingSlots, value: initialSlots)
	emitStoreField(module, block: shrink, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, value: emitConst(module, block: shrink, value: MboxRingHeadReset, ids: ids))
	module.setTerminator(shrink, op: StdOp.branch(noSender.id))

	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: noSender, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(noSender, op: StdOp.ret(emitMboxInboxAddr(module, block: noSender, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)))

	let wakeDebt = ids.mint()
	senderWoken.blockArgs.push(IrBlockArg.create(wakeDebt, argType: StdType.i64))
	emitSchedWakeIfOwed(module, cur: senderWoken, owed: wakeDebt, wake: senderWake, cont: senderPaid, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(senderPaid, op: StdOp.ret(emitMboxInboxAddr(module, block: senderPaid, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)))

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxRecvTake'

// `__mbox_close(mbox)` — make the queue un-fillable and drainable, ready every waiting sender
// `stopped`, and wake whoever is parked on it so the loop can observe that. Idempotent: both roads to it (the last handle drop, and
// `h.shutdown()`) may run, in either order.
function buildMboxClose(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxCloseName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var drainSenders = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closedrainsenders", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var stopSender = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closestopsender", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var sendersDrained = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closesendersdrained", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var handoff = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closewakeparked", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var nobodyParked = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closenoreceiver", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var doneBlock = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxwoken", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var readyLoop = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closereadyloop", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var readyOne = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closereadyone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var readied = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closereadied", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var settled = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closesettled", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var payWake = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closepaywake", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var finished = module.addBlock(func, label: b"closefinished", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let mbox = 0

	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffClosed, value: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxIsClosed, ids: ids))
	let sendRoot = emitMboxSendRoot(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	let noDebt = emitConst(module, block: entry, value: WakeDebtNone, ids: ids)
	emitBranchCarrying(module, from: entry, to: drainSenders, value: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxChainEnd, ids: ids))

	// Every waiting sender is claimed and unlinked in this one hold, so no receive can deliver a
	// later sender into the closed mailbox; they are readied from a private chain after the leave.

	let chain = ids.mint()
	drainSenders.blockArgs.push(IrBlockArg.create(chain, argType: StdType.i64))
	let waiting = emitMboxClaimFrontSender(module, func: func, scan: drainSenders, root: sendRoot, outcome: MboxSendWake.stopped, empty: sendersDrained, won: stopSender, carried: argsOf(chain), ids: ids)

	emitMboxSendUnlink(module, block: stopSender, sender: waiting, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: stopSender, record: waiting, offset: GtOffSendNext, value: chain)
	emitBranchCarrying(module, from: stopSender, to: drainSenders, value: waiting)

	let parked = emitMboxBranchOnParkedReceiver(module, cur: sendersDrained, mbox: mbox, noReceiver: nobodyParked, handoff: handoff, ids: ids)
	emitMboxWakeParked(module, func: func, cur: handoff, mbox: mbox, parked: parked, handed: emitConst(module, block: handoff, value: MboxNoHandedMessage, ids: ids), cont: doneBlock, ids: ids)

	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: nobodyParked, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(nobodyParked, op: StdOp.branch(doneBlock.id))

	module.setTerminator(doneBlock, op: StdOp.branch(readyLoop.id))
	doneBlock.branchEdges.push(BranchEdge.create(readyLoop.id, argIds: twoArgs(chain, second: noDebt)))

	let link = ids.mint()
	let owed = ids.mint()
	readyLoop.blockArgs.push(IrBlockArg.create(link, argType: StdType.i64))
	readyLoop.blockArgs.push(IrBlockArg.create(owed, argType: StdType.i64))
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: readyLoop, value: link, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxChainEnd, whenTrue: settled, whenFalse: readyOne, ids: ids)

	// The link is read and zeroed before the ready: a readied sender may park on another queue at
	// once, and its `GtOffSendNext` is then that queue's.
	let following = emitLoadField(module, block: readyOne, record: link, offset: GtOffSendNext, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: readyOne, record: link, offset: GtOffSendNext, value: emitConst(module, block: readyOne, value: MboxChainEnd, ids: ids))
	emitMboxReadyClaimedSender(module, func: func, cur: readyOne, sender: link, cont: readied, ids: ids)

	let wakeDebt = ids.mint()
	readied.blockArgs.push(IrBlockArg.create(wakeDebt, argType: StdType.i64))
	let owedNow = emitBin(module, block: readied, a: owed, b: wakeDebt, opcode: StdBinOpcode.bitOr, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(readied, op: StdOp.branch(readyLoop.id))
	readied.branchEdges.push(BranchEdge.create(readyLoop.id, argIds: twoArgs(following, second: owedNow)))

	emitSchedWakeIfOwed(module, cur: settled, owed: owed, wake: payWake, cont: finished, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(finished, op: StdOp.retVoid)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxClose'

// `__mbox_send_abandon(gt) -> wakeDebt`. See `MboxSendAbandonName`.
function buildMboxSendAbandon(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxSendAbandonName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var dequeue = module.addBlock(func, label: b"abandondequeue", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var woken = module.addBlock(func, label: b"abandonwoken", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var gone = module.addBlock(func, label: b"abandongone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let sender = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: sender, offset: GtOffParkArg, ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitMboxClaimSender(module, block: entry, sender: sender, outcome: MboxSendWake.cancelled, lost: gone, won: dequeue, ids: ids)

	emitMboxHandOffClaimedSender(module, func: func, cur: dequeue, mbox: mbox, sender: sender, cont: woken, ids: ids)

	let debt = ids.mint()
	woken.blockArgs.push(IrBlockArg.create(debt, argType: StdType.i64))
	module.setTerminator(woken, op: StdOp.ret(debt))

	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: gone, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitConstReturn(module, block: gone, value: WakeDebtNone, ids: ids)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxSendAbandon'

// `__mbox_handle_clone_box(handleBox) -> handleBox`. See `MboxHandleCloneBoxName`.
//
// ⚠ **BOTH COUNTS GO UP, AND `refs` IS NOT REDUNDANT.** `handles` decides when the mailbox CLOSES and
// `refs` when it is FREED; a clone adds a namer of the mailbox and therefore one of each. Stepping only
// `handles` would let the drop of the original free a record its clone still points at.
function buildMboxHandleCloneBox(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxHandleCloneBoxName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let handleBox = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	_ = emitMboxSharesStep(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, delta: MboxShareUnit, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(emitHandleBoxHolding(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, boxBytes: ServiceHandleBoxSize, ids: ids)))

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxHandleCloneBox'

// `__mbox_handle_destruct(handleBox)`. See `MboxHandleDestructName`.
//
// ⭐⭐ **THE ORDER IS CLOSE-THEN-RELEASE, AND REVERSING IT IS A USE-AFTER-FREE.** `__mbox_close` reads and
// writes the record, so the reference this frame holds has to outlive it — which is exactly what `refs`
// counts. So the sole handle closes first and only then gives its share back, freeing on a prior of
// `MboxShareUnit`. One combined step before the close would give up this frame's ref first, and the
// loop's exit could free the record under the close.
//
// The sole-handle test is one load, and its answer cannot go stale: a box being destroyed has
// refcount 0, so nothing mints a handle from it, and a registry slot holds a counted box. Any other
// drop gives its share back by a CAS that retries from the load, because a concurrent drop can make
// this one the sole handle.
function buildMboxHandleDestruct(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxHandleDestructName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var inspect = module.addBlock(func, label: b"destructinspect", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var dropShare = module.addBlock(func, label: b"destructdrop", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var closeIt = module.addBlock(func, label: b"destructclose", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var freeMbox = module.addBlock(func, label: b"destructfree", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var doneBlock = module.addBlock(func, label: b"destructdone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let handleBox = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.branch(inspect.id))

	let shares = emitLoadAcquireField(module, block: inspect, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffShares, ids: ids)
	let handles = emitBin(module, block: inspect, a: shares, b: emitConst(module, block: inspect, value: MboxHandleShift, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.shrLogical, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: inspect, value: handles, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxSoleHandle, whenTrue: closeIt, whenFalse: dropShare, ids: ids)

	let remaining = emitBin(module, block: dropShare, a: shares, b: emitConst(module, block: dropShare, value: MboxShareUnit, ids: ids), opcode: StdBinOpcode.sub, ids: ids)
	let dropped = emitCasField(module, block: dropShare, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffShares, expected: shares, replacement: remaining, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCasLost(module, block: dropShare, result: dropped, lost: inspect, won: doneBlock, ids: ids)

	module.appendOp(closeIt, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: MboxCloseName, args: argsOf(mbox)))
	let priorShares = emitMboxSharesStep(module, block: closeIt, mbox: mbox, delta: -MboxShareUnit, ids: ids)
	let wasLastShare = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: closeIt, value: priorShares, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxShareUnit, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(closeIt, op: StdOp.condBranch(wasLastShare, thenBlockId: freeMbox.id, elseBlockId: doneBlock.id))

	var regionFreed = emitMboxFreeRegion(module, func: func, cur: freeMbox, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(regionFreed, op: StdOp.branch(doneBlock.id))

	module.setTerminator(doneBlock, op: StdOp.retVoid)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxHandleDestruct'

// `__mbox_service_exit(mbox)` — the loop's last act. See `MboxServiceExitName`.
//
// ⚠⚠ **THE CONSUMER TICKET IS ADDED FROM INSIDE THE GREEN THREAD, AND ADDING IT AT THE SPAWN INSTEAD WOULD
// BE A TOMBSTONE.** A service has no promise, so nobody else will ever call `__gt_owner_done` for it — the
// thread is its own consumer. But `emitGtIsDropped` reads exactly that ticket to mean *"the promise is gone,
// do not RUN this thread"*, so a ticket added at spawn would make a never-yet-run service read as abandoned
// to every popper (`GtRuntime.emitGtIsDropped`). Added here it is the honest statement it looks like: this
// thread is finished, and the strand runner that switched into it supplies the runner's half.
//
// ⭐⭐ **THE GREEN THREAD IS READ HERE AND IS NOT A PARAMETER, BECAUSE THE MAXON-TIER LOOP HAS NO WAY TO NAME
// ONE.** `<T>.__loop` is ordinary program code (`ServiceLoop`) — its two parameters are the state and the
// mailbox, and there is no expression in the language that means "the green thread I am running on". Taking
// it as a parameter therefore left the loop passing ONE argument to a two-parameter entry, and `rdx` carried
// whatever the preceding `__mm_decref` left in it straight into `__gt_owner_done`. **MEASURED: a service
// whose state has TWO fields segfaulted where the same program with one field ran clean** — the difference
// being only which garbage the state's drop happened to leave behind.
//
// ⚠ `emitLoadCurrentGt`'s precondition — the scheduler is initialized — is satisfied by construction and not
// by convention: this function's only caller is a body RUNNING on a green thread the scheduler created.
function buildMboxServiceExit(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxServiceExitName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var freeMbox = module.addBlock(func, label: b"exitfree", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var doneBlock = module.addBlock(func, label: b"exitdone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let mbox = 0
	let selfGt = emitLoadCurrentGt(module, block: entry, ids: ids)

	let priorShares = emitMboxSharesStep(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, delta: -MboxRefUnit, ids: ids)
	let wasLastRef = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: entry, value: priorShares, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxLastRefOnly, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.condBranch(wasLastRef, thenBlockId: freeMbox.id, elseBlockId: doneBlock.id))

	var regionFreed = emitMboxFreeRegion(module, func: func, cur: freeMbox, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(regionFreed, op: StdOp.branch(doneBlock.id))

	module.appendOp(doneBlock, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: GtOwnerDoneName, args: argsOf(selfGt)))
	module.setTerminator(doneBlock, op: StdOp.retVoid)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxServiceExit'

function buildMboxReplyRefused(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxReplyRefusedName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param(), needsGreenThreadStackGuard: true, pinsItsThread: true)
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let cell = 0
	let noResult = emitConst(module, block: entry, value: 0, ids: ids)
	let refused = emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxRefusedReplyFlag, ids: ids)

	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: GtCellCompleteName, args: threeArgs(cell, second: noResult, third: refused)))
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: GtPromiseDropName, args: argsOf(cell)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.retVoid)
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxReplyRefused'

function buildMboxUnknownTag(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxUnknownTagName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 0, paramTypes: StdTypeArray.create())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(0)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.cold)
	emitRuntimeAbort(module, func: func, block: entry, abort: RuntimeAbort.serviceLoopUnknownMessageTag, ids: ids)
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxUnknownTag'

// The second half of `__mbox_recv`'s park, run by `__gt_run_strand` on the receiver's own OS
// thread. Both stores precede the leave: a send marks `GtOffParkArg` and readies the thread as soon
// as it takes the lock, and a store after that would erase the mark or make a readied thread
// `waiting`.
export function emitMboxParkCommit(module StdModule, block IrBlock, gt ValueId, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: gt, offset: GtOffParkArg, value: emitConst(module, block: block, value: MboxNoHandedMessage, ids: ids))
	emitMboxParkWaiting(module, block: block, gt: gt, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxParkCommit'

function emitMboxParkWaiting(module StdModule, block IrBlock, gt ValueId, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	emitGtMarkWaiting(module, block: block, gt: gt, ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxParkWaiting'

// The second half of `__mbox_send_queue`'s park, run as `emitMboxParkCommit` is. `waiting` and the
// timer precede the leave, because a waker that takes the lock may release the sender at once.
export function emitMboxSendParkCommit(module StdModule, func IrFunction, block IrBlock, gt ValueId, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns IrBlock
	var arm = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendparkarm", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var unbounded = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendparkunbounded", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var committed = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendparkcommitted", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	let deadline = emitLoadField(module, block: block, record: gt, offset: GtOffSendDeadline, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: block, value: deadline, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: GtDeadlineMaxNs, whenTrue: unbounded, whenFalse: arm, ids: ids)

	var armed = emitGtArmTimerDeadline(module, func: func, cur: arm, gt: gt, deadline: deadline, tag: TimerTagSend, ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: armed, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(armed, op: StdOp.branch(committed.id))

	emitMboxParkWaiting(module, block: unbounded, gt: gt, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(unbounded, op: StdOp.branch(committed.id))

	return committed
end 'emitMboxSendParkCommit'
